Track 1: Azimuth Creep
- Story & Context: When the auxiliary generator sputtered dry at the dry-lake truck stop of Bir Qattar, sound-trader Layla pryed open an aluminum flight case containing an unspooled 1984 quarter-inch master tape crusted with white alkali dust. She spliced the brittle magnetic ribbon with electrical tape while the wind rattled the corrugated iron roof, feeding the playback through a battery-rigged UK 2-step garage sampler while her sister picked out cold, cyclical arpeggios on an unvarnished nylon harp. The crowd fell dead quiet as the grinding grime sub-bass rattled the chai glasses against the tin counter, and Layla leaned over the CB mic to chant, "we trade the copper when the road turns white."
