Track 3: Floppy Disks Swallow the Salt
- Story & Context: Years after the northern caravan tracks were abandoned by the diesel haulers, desert nomads began reporting that the salt crust near the Zarzaitine basin vibrated with a continuous forty-hertz rumble whenever the night winds blew through discarded equipment caches. Scavengers searching the dunes uncovered a plastic crate of water-damaged 3.5-inch diskettes, their magnetic platters encrusted in gypsum crystals that produced shimmering modal harp loops and ghosted breakbeats when forced into an optical tape scanner. Old haulers around the campfire still warn greenhorn drivers that lingering near the cache will shake loose the bolts in their axles, humming the eerie transmitted hook: "leave your iron at the bottom of the dune."
